# Allowlist: only the product is tracked. Anything else you place at the root
# (your instance, your project repos, scratch folders) is invisible to this
# repo's git.
/*
!/framework/
!/tools/
!/LIFTOFF.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/LICENSE
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes

# .claude ships ONLY its skills (auto-discovered on clone); session-local
# files (settings.local.json, caches) must never be tracked.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/

# operator-local; never ships
tools/leak-sweep.private.txt

# The operator's instance, in full. A liftoff writes everything that is THIS
# operator's into _command/: the doctrine overlay, founder profile, portfolio
# spokes, task boards and ticket folders, learning log, daily pointer, machine
# profile. None of it is the product, and a spoke for a confidential front
# describes work under someone else's NDA, so none of it may be committed from a
# clone of this repo, which is public. Version it, if you want history for it, in
# a private repo of your own.
#
# The allowlist above already excludes it. Stated again here, and deliberately
# AFTER the allowlist, so that a negation added up there by mistake cannot put it
# back. tools/check-ignores.ps1 asserts it.
/_command/

# founder's internal project docs (allowlist already excludes; explicit for safety)
.project/

# optional fronts/ container: host your project repos here (moved or copied in),
# each keeping its own git, invisible to this repo via the allowlist. Explicit
# for clarity. See framework/task-board.md (front placement).
fronts/

# Ticket payloads. A ticket folder is tasks/<ID>-<slug>/, and only two things in
# it are ever worth versioning: the record and the scripts. Everything else it
# accumulates - samples, artifacts, screenshots, and whatever name a future
# session invents - is payload and stays local.
#
# So exclude the folder's contents and re-include those two, rather than listing
# the payload directories by name. A named list fails open on the first name
# nobody thought of, and this rule has to hold for confidential fronts, where
# failing open means committing someone else's data. Same shape as the .claude/
# rule above.
#
# The scope is the children of any directory named tasks, one level down. So
# tasks/_board.md is untouched, and a samples/ or artifacts/ directory anywhere
# ELSE in product code is untouched. It does mean product code must not sit two
# levels under a directory named tasks: framework/tasks/queue/worker.py would be
# ignored. tools/check-ignores.ps1 asserts both directions.
**/tasks/*/*
!**/tasks/*/ticket.md
!**/tasks/*/scripts/

# retired location, kept ignored on purpose. Payloads used to live in a sibling
# .tickets/<ID>-<slug>/ tree (MC-003, superseded by MC-005). An instance whose
# spokes still name that path must not be able to commit what it writes there, and
# those spokes live outside this repo where this change cannot reach them.
.tickets/

# generated by the optional docs-viewer skill (any depth)
node_modules/
.docs-viewer-cache/
